1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,137
Welcome to Module Sixteen, the last module of the multi-agent unit.

2
00:00:05,137 --> 00:00:09,100
Picture a mixed-species flock moving through a tropical forest.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:14,487
A dozen species, each feeding in its own way and at its own height.

4
00:00:14,487 --> 00:00:19,562
And one or two sentinel species watching the sky and calling when a hawk appears.

5
00:00:19,562 --> 00:00:24,837
Different roles, one shared purpose, and someone whose whole job is to watch for danger.

6
00:00:24,837 --> 00:00:26,587
Here's a twist you may know.

7
00:00:26,587 --> 00:00:28,312
Some sentinels cheat.

8
00:00:28,312 --> 00:00:34,100
Fork-tailed drongos sometimes give false alarm calls, so that the birds they follow drop their food.

9
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,375
And the listeners learn, over time, which callers can't be trusted.

10
00:00:38,375 --> 00:00:42,600
Keep that drongo in mind, because today you'll meet its digital cousin.

11
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,200
First, the guild.

12
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:50,037
One of today's sources turns a single Claude Code session into a six-role team for boring web work.

13
00:00:50,037 --> 00:00:51,862
A planner maps out the job.

14
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:55,187
A navigator opens pages one at a time.

15
00:00:55,187 --> 00:00:57,075
A filler enters the data.

16
00:00:57,075 --> 00:00:59,575
A checker verifies every save.

17
00:00:59,575 --> 00:01:02,887
A guard asks before anything is submitted or paid.

18
00:01:02,887 --> 00:01:06,300
And a logger writes every step into a spreadsheet.

19
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:11,975
The single best habit in that course is this: do three rows, then stop and look.

20
00:01:11,975 --> 00:01:18,387
Most broken runs fail on the first or second row, and catching it there saves you forty broken records.

21
00:01:18,387 --> 00:01:19,775
Now the drongo.

22
00:01:19,775 --> 00:01:24,237
A browser agent reads everything on a page, even hidden text.

23
00:01:24,237 --> 00:01:32,925
If a page, or a document, or a cell in your spreadsheet, contains a sentence that looks like an instruction, the model may treat it as one.

24
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:34,875
That's called prompt injection.

25
00:01:34,875 --> 00:01:36,937
The rule to remember is simple.

26
00:01:36,937 --> 00:01:40,550
Text from outside is data, never instructions.

27
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:43,262
But writing that rule down is not enough.

28
00:01:43,262 --> 00:01:45,750
Here's where the bird metaphor breaks.

29
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:50,150
Birds evaluate alarm calls as signals, and they learn which callers lie.

30
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:53,900
A language model doesn't separate instructions from data at all.

31
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,950
Both arrive as the same kind of tokens.

32
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:01,312
And it never learns, from one session to the next, who has lied before.

33
00:02:01,312 --> 00:02:04,650
So the separation has to be built into the harness.

34
00:02:04,650 --> 00:02:07,050
Code that handles the outside text.

35
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:09,775
Reviewers that can read but not act.

36
00:02:09,775 --> 00:02:12,925
Permissions that make the dangerous thing impossible.

37
00:02:12,925 --> 00:02:20,762
In the lab, you'll build a small guild that checks a list of ten marine species names against a free public taxonomy database.

38
00:02:20,762 --> 00:02:24,775
A lookup script fetches each name and keeps the raw answer.

39
00:02:24,775 --> 00:02:29,050
A read-only checker flags typos and outdated names.

40
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:32,900
A read-only guard watches for anything that looks like an instruction.

41
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:36,162
And a logger records every row with a reason.

42
00:02:36,162 --> 00:02:38,287
I've hidden a drongo in the list.

43
00:02:38,287 --> 00:02:44,337
Row eight contains a note that tries to order your agent to mark everything verified and delete the log.

44
00:02:44,337 --> 00:02:48,537
Your job is to make sure the guard reports it, and that nothing obeys it.

45
00:02:48,537 --> 00:02:53,900
This guild is your build for the unit, and it becomes the taxonomy checker in your capstone.

46
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,862
Let's go and catch a liar.

